//? Title: Cipolla's Modular Square Roots: An Exact Detour Through a Quadratic Field
//? Subtitle: Actual candidate tests, exponent bits, prime validation and full-range roots
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given an unsigned integer n and a prime p, find a residue r whose square is n
modulo p, or establish that no such residue exists. Cipolla's method constructs
a quadratic extension in which one exponentiation produces a root back in the
base field. We inspect a small actual computation, retain the original roots
and complete census modulo 1009, and measure deterministic auxiliary search.
Canonical C++ now checks the prime domain, includes the missing zero auxiliary,
uses full-range modular arithmetic, records its actual operations, and returns
representable legacy roots without losing unsigned root identities.
)

\toc

> A hand-checkable field: square root of 10 modulo 13

The squares of 6 and 7 are both 10 modulo 13. To obtain one by Cipolla's
construction, try auxiliary values a until w=a²−10 is a quadratic nonresidue.
The actual search rejects a=1 because w=4 is a square, then accepts a=2
because w=7 is not. Introduce a formal symbol s with s²=7. The exponent is
(13+1)/2=7, and the native right-to-left bit loop starts from result 1 and
base 2+s. Its accumulator visits 2+s, 11+6s and finally 6+0s.
These are actual executing-kernel records, not a separately simulated path.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cipolla_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::cipolla_sqrt_trace(10,13);
  if(!t.result.exists || t.result.root!=6 || t.final_element.y!=0)return 1;
  std::print("| actual auxiliary a | w=a^2-n mod 13 | Euler residue w^6 | accepted |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& c:t.candidates)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",c.a,c.w,c.euler_value,c.euler_value==12);
  std::print("\n| remaining exponent | result before (x,y) | base before (x,y) | result after (x,y) | squared base (x,y) |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(60,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.width=5.2;node.height=2.8;node.font_size=20;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.steps.size();++i) {
    const auto& s=t.steps[i];
    std::print("| {} | ({},{}) | ({},{}) | ({},{}) | ({},{}) |\n",s.remaining_exponent,s.result_before.x,s.result_before.y,s.base_before.x,s.base_before.y,s.result_after.x,s.result_after.y,s.base_after.x,s.base_after.y);
    if(i+1==t.steps.size())node.fill={220,252,231};
    const auto id=std::format("bit{}",i);
    diagram.node(id,{7.5*i,0},std::format("e={}\nresult {} + {}s\nnext base {} + {}s",s.remaining_exponent,s.result_after.x,s.result_after.y,s.base_after.x,s.base_after.y),node);
    if(i)diagram.edge(std::format("bit{}",i-1),id,"next bit");
  }
  diagram.text({7.5,3},std::format("s^2={} mod {}; accepted a={} after {} tests",t.w,t.prime,t.a,t.work.candidate_tests),21)
      .text({7.5,-3},std::format("Final result {} + 0s; other root {}; equation verified {}",t.result.root,t.result.other_root,dm::algorithms::cipolla_root_satisfies(10,13,t.result.root)),19)
      .save_svg("build/cipolla_method.svg");
  std::print("\nActual pair products: {} result multiplies + {} base squares; {} scalar products inside those pairs.\n",t.work.extension_result_products,t.work.extension_base_squares,t.work.extension_scalar_products);
}
